PATCH 504: the whole 209e cockpit paint/input method family base-lost the player near offset.

DAT_2000_2d34 (DGROUP:0x6d34) holds the PLAYER object's NEAR OFFSET -- FUN_0000_466c stores it that way
(patch 300) -- and every member of this family dereferenced it as a host pointer.  The group splits in
two shapes, both dispatched by the 209e display-list walk (patch 142):

  INPUT handlers (80b5, 8123, 816d, 81b7, 820b): `test ax,0x80; je -> stc` / `test ax,1; jne -> clc`,
  then act on the player object.  All five also dropped the clc/stc contract the walk consumes.
      80b5  turret centre:  bit2 -> word[di+0x8b]=0, bit4 -> 0x8000, both then a2a8 (already near-offset,
            patch 261).
      8123  weapon select:  `mov si,[bx+2]; movb [bp+si],3`, and on bits 0x14
            `mov al,[bp+si+1]; mov [di+0x86],al; lcall 0f69:8999` (== linear 0x18029, FUN_1000_8029).
      816d  hatch:          byte[di+0xc9]=3, byte[di+0x3e]=6 (or 0 on bits 0x14/0x400).
      81b7  816d's twin:    byte[di+0xca]=3, byte[di+0x3e]=8.
      820b  fire:           byte[di+0xde]=byte[di+0xdf]=3, then aae8 + `orb [di+0x17],0x80`, else
            `andb [di+0x17],0x7f`.

  PAINT methods (80eb, 819c, 81e6, 8243; 8152 was patch 503): they run with BX = the display-list
  element's near offset and BP = the walk base.  The walk publishes BX to DGROUP:0x3e08 (`mov [0x3e08],bx`)
  and BP to g_fist_paintbp (patch 142), and the port's dispatch is arg-less, so both are read back from
  there.  Ghidra dereferenced the element as a host pointer, emitted the `addw/subw [bx+2],K` pairs as
  4-byte int read-modify-writes, and dropped the (ax,bx) argument pair of every `lcall [0x6b4]`.
      80eb  weapon-select plate: glyph base 0x3d8/0x3e8/0x3f8 by byte[bp+[bx+2]+1], +8 if it matches
            byte[di+0x86] else + byte[di+0x3f].
      819c  8152's twin: byte[di+0x3f]+0x418, offset 0x2f.
      81e6  two-glyph gauge: (byte[di+0x3f]+0x428, 0x90d6) then (byte[di+0x3f]+0x438, 0x90de).
      8243  weapon-station plate: `mov bl,[bp+si+1]; mov ax,[bx-0x6f1a]` -- a WORD at DGROUP:(0x90e6+bl),
            the index UNSCALED because the stored ids are pre-scaled -- then +8 if bl == byte[di+0x91]
            else + byte[di+0x3f].

None of this could run before patches 499-503 let the player-death path complete and the post-death
event drain reach the display-list walk.
